 {r}←Shutdown INI;event;timeout
⍝ Kills all threads except thread 0 and the current one, Rumba's included, closes all Conga connections,
⍝ sends the quit event to the root, unties all files, and finally calls `OFF`.
⍝ The threads are killed first so that none of them is still working with Conga when it is closed.
⍝ `INI` is either ⍬ (or '') or an instance of the Plodder INI file. If it is an instance with an entry
⍝ [EVENTS]QuitEvent, that event is sent to the root.
⍝ Like `OFF` it does not quit in a development environment unless the command line carries OFF=1;
⍝ it then just returns.
 r←⍬
 WindowsEventLog'Shutting down'
 {}⎕TKILL ⎕TNUMS~0,⎕TID                     ⍝ Kill everything but thread 0 and this one
 timeout←5000+3⊃⎕AI
 :While 0<≢⎕TNUMS~0,⎕TID                    ⍝ A thread in a Conga call dies only when that call returns
 :AndIf timeout>3⊃⎕AI
     ⎕DL 0.1
 :EndWhile
 :If 9=##.⎕NC'RumbaLean.DRC'                ⍝ Rumba's `InitConga` establishes DRC in RumbaLean, not in Core
     {}##.RumbaLean.DRC.Close'.'
 :EndIf
 {}##.⎕EX'RumbaLean.DRC'
 :If 9=⎕NC'INI'
 :AndIf INI.Exist'EVENTS:QuitEvent'
     event←INI.Get'EVENTS:QuitEvent'
     :Trap 11                               ⍝ An invalid event name in the INI file must not stop the shutdown
         r←⎕NQ'.'event
     :EndTrap
 :EndIf
 ⎕FUNTIE ⎕FNUMS
 ⎕NUNTIE ⎕NNUMS
 OFF
⍝Done
